pseudo-Boolean proof version 3.0
% Positive companion to
% incorrect/version3/strengthening_to_core_deletion_proofgoal_not_contradiction:
% a checked deletion under `strengthening_to_core on` is a proof by
% contradiction with no database obligations, and this is what discharging it
% legitimately looks like. Deleting `1 x1 1 x2 >= 1` leaves `1 x1 >= 1`, which
% together with the negated deleted constraint propagates to conflict, so the
% subproof's top-level RUP check succeeds and the deletion is licensed.
f 2;
strengthening_to_core on;
del id 2 : : subproof
qed;
output NONE;
conclusion NONE;
end pseudo-Boolean proof;
